diff --git a/docs/hardware/macbook71-function-keys.md b/docs/hardware/macbook71-function-keys.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..54fffd4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/hardware/macbook71-function-keys.md
@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+# MacBook7,1 function keys
+
+This change adds an opt-in-by-hardware-identity keyboard path and a native
+RenkuOS MCP89 panel backlight driver. It does not install nouveau, port NVIDIA's
+proprietary Linux driver, or add GeForce 320M modesetting/3D acceleration to the
+older Haiku `nvidia` graphics driver. The existing EFI framebuffer continues to
+provide display output.
+
+## Hardware gate
+
+The USB quirk requires all of:
+
+- SMBIOS vendor `Apple Inc.` and product exactly `MacBook7,1`;
+- built-in ANSI keyboard USB VID/PID `05ac:0236`, interface 0;
+- Apple Fn field at usage page `0x00ff`, usage `0x0003`, in its keyboard report.
+
+A missing SMBIOS string must fail matching. The prerequisite SMBIOS fix also
+retains the existing NULL-query wildcard semantics. Sharing the same keyboard
+USB ID on a different Mac is not enough to activate this quirk. ISO/JIS variants
+are not enabled without descriptor/hardware evidence.
+
+The backlight driver separately checks that exact SMBIOS identity, PCI VGA
+`10de:08a0`, a memory BAR with enough space, enabled memory decoding, NVAF chipset
+identity `0xaf`, and a live, internally consistent PWM pair. It never offers a
+force-load override. Only the PWM page is writable; no userspace MMIO mapping is
+exported. Invalid firmware/hardware state leaves the backlight unavailable.
+
+## Key behavior
+
+| Key | Without Fn | With Fn |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| F1 / F2 | Panel brightness -5 / +5 percentage points | F1 / F2 |
+| F3 | Open Workspaces | F3 |
+| F4 | Open the system Applications folder in Tracker | F4 |
+| F5 / F6 | F5 / F6 (no keyboard backlight on this model) | F5 / F6 |
+| F7 / F8 / F9 | MediaPlayer previous / play-pause / next | F7 / F8 / F9 |
+| F10 / F11 / F12 | System mute / volume down / volume up | F10 / F11 / F12 |
+
+F3/F4 are RenkuOS equivalents chosen for the printed window/dashboard keys;
+this does not implement macOS Exposé or Dashboard. Media keys target the first
+window of an already running MediaPlayer, not arbitrary third-party players.
+The separate optical eject key and Fn+navigation keys are outside this patch.
+
+Translations are latched per physical function key until release. Changing Fn
+while holding a key cannot turn its repeat or key-up into a different key.
+The USB driver emits private raw codes, so the filter does not intercept regular
+F-keys or generic consumer keys from other keyboards. F5/F6 pass through.
+Actions run on a worker looper, not the input dispatch thread. Only brightness
+and volume repeat; repeated mute/play/launch actions are suppressed. Stale
+repeats are discarded and repeats are limited to ten per second.
+
+## NVIDIA register evidence and licensing
+
+The existing local Linux setup is documented in `machine/macbook-linux`, which
+points to [macbook-mint-nvidia-revival](https://github.com/rainygirl/macbook-mint-nvidia-revival),
+commit `f438b4e0caf7265813b22c080198919ca4dc1de1`.
+Its `mcp89-backlight/mcp89_backlight.c` records measurements on this machine:
+
+- BAR0 + `0x61c080`: existing PWM period; never written by the new driver.
+- BAR0 + `0x61c084`: low 24 bits are duty; bit 31 must be set on each write to
+  latch a change. Readback bit 30 is hardware maintained.
+- The observed Linux periods were 2966 and 24557; the implementation uses the
+  current period rather than either hardcoded value.
+
+That Linux module is GPL-2.0. No Linux module source, callbacks, Linux headers,
+or NVIDIA binary code is included here. The native implementation is new MIT
+code using the recorded register facts, PCI module APIs and device hooks.
+
+## Build
+
+From a configured RenkuOS x86_64 build directory, with the complete series
+applied to its source tree:
+
+```sh
+jam -q -j4 smbios usb_hid i2c_hid mcp89_backlight macbook71_keys
+```
+
+`i2c_hid` is included because it compiles the shared keyboard handler. The
+backlight is listed in regular x86_64 images, and the input filter in the Haiku
+package. The package/image targets also need validation before merge.
+
+## Tests and current validation limits
+
+Run the host tests from the source root:
+
+```sh
+python3 src/tests/add-ons/macbook71/run_tests.py
+```
+
+These compile the real translation helper and extracted production SMBIOS/
+backlight ioctl functions, with host-only type and kernel/MMIO mocks, under
+AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. They test all F-key mappings,
+Fn transitions, repeats, simultaneous keys, ordinary key pass-through, exact
+machine matches including missing strings, bounded PWM arithmetic, the write
+latch, unchanged period and invalid PWM/argument handling. These are not a
+native kernel build or hardware validation.
+
+As of 2026-10-16:
+
+- Read-only SSH inspection confirmed USB `05ac:0236`, PCI `10de:08a0` and the
+  active `/dev/graphics/framebuffer` path on the target.
+- Native x86_64 builds of all five targets pass. A missing `vm/vm.h` include
+  found by the native build was corrected. The Linux ASan/UBSan host suite passes.
+- The actual 156-byte HID descriptor contains Fn usage `0x00ff0003` in report 1.
+  PMC_BOOT_0 reads `0x0af000a2`; PWM period/duty read `0x00000b98`/`0x000008f1`.
+- The native driver was installed and its real ioctl path changed brightness
+  from 77% to 72% and restored 77%. A GET also succeeded after an independent
+  machine reboot. Actual luminance still requires user visual confirmation.
+- USB HID, SMBIOS and filter overrides were installed after saving the packaged
+  originals. After requesting an input_server restart, SSH became unavailable;
+  physical keyboard/panel verification and post-restart state are still pending.
+  This session did not reboot the machine or modify Wi-Fi files.
+
+Before considering the change ready to merge, build all targets and an image;
+confirm the gates on a different model and with missing SMBIOS strings; inspect
+the descriptor and PWM on MacBook7,1; exercise every row in the table, Fn release
+ordering, multi-key holds, modifier combinations, held mute/play keys, ordinary
+external keyboard F-keys, brightness endpoints, MediaPlayer absent/present,
+restart, reboot and suspend/resume. Verify actual panel luminance, not just MMIO
+readback. The backlight does not add persistence or suspend callbacks in this
+series; it reads the live period and rejects invalid state on each ioctl.
+
+The patch is a reviewable draft until native build and hardware checks pass.
